   {"mm": [144.0, 271.8, 166.2, 276.9], "text": "(83 mm"},
   {"mm": [178.8, 271.8, 198.2, 276.9], "text": "86 mm"},
   {"mm": [211.2, 271.8, 236.4, 276.9], "text": "15 mm)."},
   {"mm": [55.1, 258.2, 296.6, 263.3], "text": "The 8-109 comprises two amplifier sections, one cons ist ing of 21 wit"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 251.5, 247.6, 256.6], "text": "01 through 04, and the other of 22 with 05 through 08"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 238.6, 225.2, 243.6], "text": "The linear integrated circuit 21 operates as"},
   {"mm": [242.7, 238.6, 301.0, 243.6], "text": "preamplifier and"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 231.9, 266.2, 236.9], "text": "buffer stage to drive the transistor output amplifier section."},
   {"mm": [55.9, 218.5, 201.0, 223.5], "text": "In the major ity of the 8-109. models, the"},
   {"mm": [231.2, 218.5, 301.6, 223.5], "text": "of the two ampl ifier"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 211.8, 164.5, 216.8], "text": "sections are interconnected as"},
   {"mm": [180.7, 211.8, 227.6, 216.8], "text": "cross coupled"},
   {"mm": [237.9, 211.8, 301.4, 216.8], "text": "ifferential pair to"},
   {"mm": [59.2, 205.1, 79.5, 210.1], "text": "ro vide"},
   {"mm": [93.3, 205.1, 122.4, 210.1], "text": "balanced"},
   {"mm": [152.6, 205.1, 301.0, 210.1], "text": "Alternately, in the case of the 8-109A and"},
   {"mm": [78.4, 198.4, 161.1, 203.4], "text": "ingl e-ended, unbalanced"},
   {"mm": [187.0, 198.4, 213.7, 203.4], "text": "is used."},
   {"mm": [55.3, 185.2, 178.8, 190.3], "text": "The balanced input yields severa"},
   {"mm": [188.5, 185.2, 301.4, 190.3], "text": "input characteristics similar to"},
   {"mm": [55.3, 178.5, 300.7, 183.6], "text": "those of an input transformer. Output level remains constant when"},
   {"mm": [55.3, 172.1, 160.6, 177.1], "text": "the input is fed from either"},
   {"mm": [175.3, 172.1, 300.3, 177.1], "text": "balanced or an unbalanced source."},
   {"mm": [55.1, 165.4, 301.0, 170.4], "text": "Good common mode rejection is another feature of this ype of input"},
   {"mm": [54.8, 158.9, 101.5, 163.9], "text": "configuration."},
   {"mm": [55.3, 145.5, 143.6, 150.6], "text": "For amplifiers operating"},
   {"mm": [163.9, 145.5, 300.7, 150.6], "text": "the balanced mode, the value of R15"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 139.0, 301.0, 144.1], "text": "establ ishes the feed back ratio of the two amplifier sect ions and"},
   {"mm": [55.3, 132.3, 168.4, 137.4], "text": "thus controls the amplifier gain."},
   {"mm": [55.3, 119.0, 103.0, 124.0], "text": "When utilized"},
   {"mm": [123.7, 119.0, 301.4, 124.0], "text": "the unbalanced arrangement, the lower amplifier"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 112.3, 171.6, 117.3], "text": "section (22 with 05 through 08)"},
   {"mm": [189.3, 112.3, 301.0, 117.3], "text": "used as the input section, with"},
   {"mm": [55.3, 105.8, 153.7, 110.8], "text": "the input signal applied to"},
   {"mm": [163.2, 105.8, 300.7, 110.8], "text": "in E2. Amplifier gain is determ ined by"},
   {"mm": [55.3, 99.1, 301.0, 104.1], "text": "the values of R6, Rll and R12. One half of the balanced output"},
   {"mm": [55.1, 92.6, 118.7, 97.7], "text": "signal appears at"},
   {"mm": [129.3, 92.6, 301.0, 97.7], "text": "in E6. The upper half of the amplif ier (21 with"},
   {"mm": [55.3, 85.9, 151.8, 91.0], "text": "01 through 04) operates as"},
   {"mm": [165.4, 85.9, 300.3, 91.0], "text": "unity ga rn inverting amplifier with El"},
   {"mm": [54.8, 79.5, 149.6, 84.5], "text": "externally strapped to E6."},
   {"mm": [55.1, 66.1, 301.0, 71.1], "text": "The output of all models of he 8-109 series is actively balanced and"},
   {"mm": [285.4, 59.2, 306.4, 68.3], "text": "ps"},
   {"mm": [65.0, 59.8, 174.2, 64.8], "text": "brought out at pi ns E4 and E6."},
